  "body": "## What changed\n- The three pixel snapshot tests (`egui_shell_snapshot`, `egui_shell_snapshot_light`, `tool_editor_snapshot`) move to the release lane: `#[ignore]`d with the lane named, not deleted. They are the only tests that read or write `crates/ui/tests/snapshots/*.png`.\n- New structural twins in `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/structural.rs` (`shell_structure_dark`, `shell_structure_light`, `tool_editor_structure`):\n  - **AccessKit assertions:** the viewport toggles and radios, the property page sections, Apply/Align WCS disabled, Generate enabled, the status-strip Debug info button, no stray window, and the tool editor's fields, their order and their values.\n  - **Painted strips:** the ribbon, browser rows and dock tab titles are painted rather than widgets, so the tests check their text and coarse placement.\n  - **Light theme:** the light palette is live and passes the contrast check.\n- `scripts/gate.sh` and `scripts/gate.ps1` add a ui snapshot lane at the end of the release tier (`cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib -- --ignored snapshot`, debug, CWD `crates/ui`). Quick and batch never pass `--ignored`.\n- `AGENTS.md` Testing gains \"Pixel snapshots are release-lane\". `.claude/agents/PR-reviewer.md` and `.claude/skills/review-prs/SKILL.md` make a PNG change in a PR a blocking finding.\n- `docs/decisions/255-structural-ui-tests.md`\n\n## How tested\n- `#[test]` count in camcraft-ui: 414 before, 417 after (3 moved to ignored, 3 structural added). The ignored count goes from 3 to 6.\n- The new structural tests pass. The camcraft-ui lib suite: 291 passed.\n- `scripts/gate.sh quick upstream/main` (macOS) passes except three headless-GPU tests (`headless_run_succeeds`, `egui_headless_cli_exit_code_is_zero`, `headless_cli_exit_code_is_zero`), which fail the same way on `upstream/main` c442118 on this machine (\"No suitable graphics adapter found\"). They are environmental and untouched here.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --tests -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n- `gate.ps1` was edited but not run (no pwsh on this Mac). The `gate.sh` release dry run lists the new step.\n- The snapshot lane run by hand on macOS: `egui_shell_snapshot` passes, while `_light` (1 px over threshold) and `tool_editor` (6 px) fail on an unchanged tree. This is the cross-platform pixel noise the issue describes, now confined to the cut. Cuts should run the lane on the OS that made the goldens (Windows).\n\nChangelog: none (test/process only)\n\nFixes #255\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
